{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1532787-more-livelier-times","id":1532787,"title":"More Livelier Times","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-17T17:22:07-07:00","id":1532787,"title":"More Livelier Times","content":"Reading a book about various kingdoms that no longer exist, and I was thinking, &quot;Is it better to have a vampire game in a Dark-Ages*-setting verses say, a more contemporary-setting as the times would have more, &quot;Action&quot;? Would a game be more interesting if everyone had swords instead if everyone had guns?<br /> <br /> *Dark Ages just means any vampire game pre-Renaissance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T03:18:37-07:00","id":1532804,"title":"","content":"Vampire isn't D&amp;D with guns, much of the action is political or business in nature. It functions well in any time period for that reason. <br /> <br /> That said if you want to run Vampire as D&amp;D and give everyone swords no one is stopping you. If your group will enjoy it, do it. You won't be the first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T08:58:47-07:00","id":1532808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1532787-more-livelier-times#post1532787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading a book about various kingdoms that no longer exist, and I was thinking, &quot;Is it better to have a vampire game in a Dark-Ages*-setting verses say, a more contemporary-setting as the times would have more, &quot;Action&quot;? Would a game be more interesting if everyone had swords instead if everyone had guns?<br /> <br /> *Dark Ages just means any vampire game pre-Renaissance.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, i would like to point out that while quite useful, firearms did not on themselves make melee weapons, archery or cavalry charges irrelevant or obsolete - soldiers and officers both would still get considerable usage out of them in and out of the battlefield up to the middle 1800s, when repeating firearms and metal cartridges made them fast and reliable as we have become accostumed to think of them in contemporary times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T10:55:01-07:00","id":1532811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1532787-more-livelier-times?p=1532808#post1532808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an aside, i would like to point out that while quite useful, firearms did not on themselves make melee weapons, archery or cavalry charges irrelevant or obsolete - soldiers and officers both would still get considerable usage out of them in and out of the battlefield up to the middle 1800s, when repeating firearms and metal cartridges made them fast and reliable as we have become accostumed to think of them in contemporary times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, not to drive things too far off topic, but one could make a decent arguement that barbed wire and machine guns used together is what really made cavalry obsolete. <br /> <br /> Anyhow, as I sit here contemplating a Requiem Arthuriana, yes premodern settings are excelletn for vampire as well. They have a different tone and feel, but there is a reason Requiem for Rome and Dark Eras are so popular. If that's what floats your boat and spurs your imagination, go for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T17:01:41-07:00","id":1532826,"title":"","content":"We tend to stick around the Victorian Age &amp; The Wild West in our older games as we are fans of that time period. So have fun in creating a setting in the classical age or the early dark ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T17:35:28-07:00","id":1532878,"title":"","content":"The Middle-Ages, I've got 500 years to play around it; in Requiem, vampires are immortal and that's a lot of time. More often than not, an ST will go, night-by-night in the game secession and not take into account immortality. <br /> <br /> Prussia; Land of swamps, pagans and a crusade. Will go from heavily Slavic to heavily German. Numerous wars. Circle of Crone?<br /> <br /> Galicia: Baroque; towns of churches, synagogues and museums. A land where Polish, Jews and Ruthians (Ukrainians), all live in relative peace, but also extreme-poverty at the base of the Carpathian-Mountains. Not much happens there; Napoleon and World Wars. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1532787-more-livelier-times?p=1532804#post1532804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire isn't D&amp;D with guns, much of the action is political or business in nature. It functions well in any time period for that reason.<br /> <br /> That said if you want to run Vampire as D&amp;D and give everyone swords no one is stopping you. If your group will enjoy it, do it. You won't be the first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know; it's Cyberpunk 2020; just kidding; I was just considering that Medieval-times, might have more action, given smaller-nations, more violence and more action; that is, a greater chance to use their supernat.-powers, so to speak. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T06:24:52-07:00","id":1532903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1532787-more-livelier-times?p=1532878#post1532878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know; it's Cyberpunk 2020; just kidding; I was just considering that Medieval-times, might have more action, given smaller-nations, more violence and more action; that is, a greater chance to use their supernat.-powers, so to speak.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need more violence to use dominate, majesty, auspex, nightmare, obfuscate, animalism, or many of the bloodline disciplines. More violence really only contributes to more use of the physical disciplines. The middle ages would be a wonderful time to be a nocturnal predator that can see in the dark though, violence or no violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T11:34:23-07:00","id":1532914,"title":"","content":"The same could be said for the wild west Shadowcat as the disciplines would give kindred outlaws a wonderful edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T20:33:53-07:00","id":1532933,"title":"","content":"Vampires are terribly powerful in dark ages with requiem rules from what I have ran. The masquerade or its equivalent is far weaker, there are no guns or flamethrowers, and the biggest fear is possibly archers, since according to rules they can stake you. A fun setting we played was the Danelaw period of English history where the Viking raiders were beginning to settle and fight with the old Gallic kings as the Romans would know them since they were Celtic and Celtic or Keltoi as it was, is a Greek term so pardon my French or Frankish or Gaulish if you would. It was a time of great historic tension and opportunity if one was shrewd enough like a vampire of some age I would wager.<br /> <br /> In the Dark ages vampires have many benefits that would see heavier use, they can naturally see in the dark, there are no cameras, law enforcement is harder since modern methods are centuries away, there are very few organized police equivalents in the West after the fall of the Western Roman empire. Swords and everything available to mortals aside from fire prove a far more manageable threat, and the presence of many smaller villages could see one rising high. Culture presents a unique benefit, the Germanic tribes who spread throughout the previous imperial lands existed by a kin group structure with many personal but few formal laws, these humanity rather than law focused groups would be easier for vampires with mental disciplines to exploit. If you are going for the early Middle Ages most would be Christian due to the conversion to Arianism no relation to Aryans, Arius believed simply that Christ was created by God and not fully God which led to some deep theological conflict with Catholics on the basis of the payment of original sin. I bring this up because this is a fascinating point of tension throughout Europe as the Romans and the lands they occupied had been Catholic but the later settlers and conquerors were not, meaning that the native populations were ruled not only by a foreign but a religiously different elite. This means lots of politicking and schemes could be played on this historical tension.<br /> <br /> These games I ran were in the earlier parts of the timeline you listed and could be a logical continuation of Requiem for Rome up until the Middle Ages. I argue it is not only possible but with a historical background you could flesh out some interesting conflict rich stories.<br /> <br /> None more dark recently published a second edition variant of Requiem for Rome that you could find a good deal of use out of, as it outlines weapons, armor, and the like through the Roman period which leads into the beginning of the Dark Ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T16:59:18-07:00","id":1533583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1532787-more-livelier-times?p=1532933#post1532933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are terribly powerful in dark ages with requiem rules from what I have ran. The masquerade or its equivalent is far weaker, there are no guns or flamethrowers, and the biggest fear is possibly archers, since according to rules they can stake you. A fun setting we played was the Danelaw period of English history where the Viking raiders were beginning to settle and fight with the old Gallic kings as the Romans would know them since they were Celtic and Celtic or Keltoi as it was, is a Greek term so pardon my French or Frankish or Gaulish if you would. It was a time of great historic tension and opportunity if one was shrewd enough like a vampire of some age I would wager.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of what I'm getting at; in the actual, historical, &quot;Dark-Ages&quot;, there was little history; just like the time of ancient-Greece; the only histories, really of that era in Europe that survived is because Arabs thought Greek-history was important enough to save. As Sprauge de Camp put it, &quot;People weren't wax-figures just waiting for history to catch up to them&quot;, at that time. So little is known about the Roman-Republic that, you could have whole chronicles with all fictional-characters and fictional-families, and there's little disputing evidence to the contrary. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the Dark ages vampires have many benefits that would see heavier use, they can naturally see in the dark, there are no cameras, . . . </div> </div> </div>The, &quot;Vampires don't appear on Camera&quot;, is one rule that I keep from NWoD. It makes a lot of sense. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T12:32:25-07:00","id":1533633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1532787-more-livelier-times?p=1533583#post1533583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The, &quot;Vampires don't appear on Camera&quot;, is one rule that I keep from NWoD. It makes a lot of sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the rule in 2e. Page 60 of the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T16:55:02-07:00","id":1533667,"title":"","content":"If we ever play this setting again, we would restrict the blurred images to the Mekhet clan as it makes more storytelling sense with it being tied to the shadow clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}